WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.280
- [Narrator] What might
seem like just a cluster

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.930
of small temples surrounding
Myanmar's Kuthodaw Pagoda,

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.650
is actually the world's largest book.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:13.550
(lively, bouncy music)

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:18.060
The Kuthodaw Pagoda is a
golden temple built in 1857,

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.360
but it's what lays around
the surrounding shrines

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:21.630
that draws people near.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:27.600
In each of the 730 white
stupas, stands a marble tablet.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.280
Combined, these tablets
make up the entirety

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:34.600
of Buddha's teachings, written
in the ancient Pali language.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:39.600
Each tablet, or page from the
book, stands five feet tall

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.640
and five inches thick.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.030
The tablets were once
covered in precious jewels

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.180
and gold ink.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.230
However, after the British
invasion in the 1880s,

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:51.500
the site was looted and the
gold ink and gems were stolen.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.660
Today, the book is still accessible.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.460
The dense writing has since
been filled with black ink

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.080
so the scripture can be
read for many years to come.

00:01:07.793 --> 00:01:10.376
(bell chiming)

